The processor's cost of a pass and of a draw's table, the command words unchanged (2026-11-12, darwin-lisa session 8).

CoreAnimation's app-close animation records 49 passes and some 220 draws a command buffer (gpu-c2/d3, the "up" gesture
from Settings: 47-49 passes a buffer, 216-226 draws, 26-28 ms from a buffer made to committed). A pass costs the core
about four draws' worth of processor time: drawbench (tools/drawbench.cpp, now with PASSES, its fourth argument) puts
220 draws in 49 passes at 2036 us a frame on the host against 1110 in one pass, some 19 us a pass, and the phone's draws
run at 6 to 10 times the host's time (33-57 us against 5).

1. CommandBuffer keeps the register shadows (RegShadow) of the pass it closed last and gives them, forgotten, to the
   next pass it opens. A shadow made new for each pass resized its 1024 page slots (8 KB zeroed) and allocated some
   twenty 1 KB pages as the pass's first draw wrote its registers, then freed them all at the pass's end. A reused
   shadow is cleared by its generation, which is what a new one is: each pass still deduplicates from nothing, and
   the words are the same (drawbench's digest of every buffer's words is equal before and after, 1, 10 and 49
   passes). tests/render_test.cpp each_pass_of_a_buffer_deduplicates_from_nothing pins it: a shadow left uncleared
   fails it (the batch start's registers left out of the second pass's head).
2. encodeDraw writes each stage's texture descriptors and samplers only as far as CP_LOAD_STATE6 loads them (numTex,
   numSamp), where it zeroed all sixteen of each and then copied all sixteen over them: 3.8 KB a draw into the table,
   which on the phone is write-combined memory (HakiosGPU's default), for a CoreAnimation draw that loads some 0.8 KB.
   The rest of the table is never read. a_draw_writes_only_the_descriptors_the_command_processor_loads checks that
   what is past the loaded ones is left as it was, and that the fake GPU takes the draw.

Host (x86, this tree's 261 tests + these 2): 263 tests, the same 3 tests and 12 checks failing as before the patch
(they predate it: the unbound-buffer refusals hakios-metal-unbound-push.patch replaced). drawbench, the same words:
220 draws in 49 passes 2036 -> 1801 us a frame (-12 %), in 10 passes 1268 -> 1239, in one pass unchanged.
CommandBuffer::streamDigest (FNV-1a of the words recorded so far) is new, for drawbench and such comparisons.

